--- body ---
## Context

The current `erg update` implementation auto-runs `erg migrate` when it
detects legacy `Status:` headers in `tickets/`. That couples binary
refresh to ticket-data mutation.

0023 resolves that this coupling is too implicit. Ticket-file migration
is a reviewed content change that should remain explicit and commitable
on its own.

## Actions

1. Remove the update-time auto-migrate behavior
2. Replace it with a clear post-update hint when legacy `Status:`
   headers are detected:
   - run `erg migrate tickets/`
   - review `git diff tickets/`
   - commit the migration separately
3. Update help text / release notes / docs to describe the explicit
   workflow
4. Add tests that lock in the new contract:
   - `erg update` no longer rewrites ticket files
   - `erg update` emits the migrate hint when needed

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `erg update` no longer runs `migrate` automatically
- [ ] legacy repos receive a clear migrate handoff
- [ ] migration remains available and idempotent via `erg migrate`
- [ ] tests cover the explicit workflow
